      "note": "Codex Tibetan-first provisional machine alignment; GMR English remains verbatim. gnas is nominal in gnas kyi blos and verbal at gnas shing; blos is retained whole. Three mig shes occurrences attach respectively to normal vision, the cup organisms' own vision, and ocean organisms' vision, each with two tighter members. Only the later tshad mar is matched to valid perception; the earlier cup-organism validity clause is distributed in GMR's recast and omitted. mi bzod is also omitted: the HGM lexical evidence for unable to bear does not by itself establish imperceptible. Repeated explanatory beings/water/organisms and the extra little wording stay unwrapped. The near-god clause keeps only certain, near-gods, weapons, glasses, see and necessity; phor gang is not assigned glasses of water, and no full relation or correction is asserted. Possessive can, the first additional necessity premise, gang quantity at the close, and yod pa'i phyir remain unbanked where the English is expanded or distributed. No hgm_gloss promotion or semantic acceptance is claimed."
